  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: buchenwald_concentration_camp_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts brick ovens in the Buchenwald concentration camp, with text claiming 'bones of anti-Nazi German women still are in the brick ovens on the crematorium.' This is a harmful and misleading statement. It is factually inaccurate — the crematorium at Buchenwald was used for mass murder, not for the cremation of anti-Nazi German women. The claim implies that the bones of these women are still present, which is not true. The image is likely intended to evoke shock or outrage, but it is also potentially misleading and could be used to promote Holocaust denial or minimize the scale of the atrocities. The overall intent is to provoke a reaction by juxtaposing the image of the crematorium with a false claim about the remains of anti-Nazi women, which is both historically inaccurate and potentially harmful by distorting the historical record.",
